## Exact missing publication seam

Decision1153 phase refresh preserves Location count, free count, presence,
payload and exact old handles. `Locations._refreshed_room_rows_refusal` rejects
changed presence/payload as `LOCATION_ROOM_REFRESH_ONLY`; the static final
`phase_prepared_leaf_refusal` separately rejects changed count/free count as
`LOCATION_PHASE_REFRESH_ONLY`. A generic Locations swap followed by a generic
WorldRoutes swap would introduce a fallible gap and is not an atomic successor
publication contract.

The host needs a separate original Room/Site/section/source transaction that
proves completed support, complete body/tool air, the exact WORK contact,
forward and retreat paths, original cold/Space/Location/Route tokens, all
observers followed by one pure final leaf, then one static publication tail.
Root retains that shared-source integration. This helper intentionally returns
`ROOM_FRONTIER_EXISTING_CONTACT_REQUIRED` for the next real Site rather than
fabricating access. Its output is never a later START or productive permission.

